   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "HI everyone,<div><br></div><div>this is a direct report from stack overflor: <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/9502003/ggplot-scale-y-log10-issue\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/9502003/ggplot-scale-y-log10-issue&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792376775856000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1i1wX35Pdna9AyPdFVNRol\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/9502003/ggplot-scale-y-log10-issue</a></div><div><br></div><div>however I think the issue has reached the point where I think I have exposed a bug (as opposed to me not knowing how to use ggplot). basically the scale becomes wrong when the fill variable is different from the x-variable for ggplot bar graphs. In the following examples, example1 will have the appropriate scale but example 2 will  not: </div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:18px;text-align:left\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:18px;text-align:left\">example_1 = ggplot(diamonds, aes(x=clarity, fill=clarity)) + geom_bar() + scale_y_log10(); print(example_1)</span><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:18px;text-align:left\">example_2 = ggplot(diamonds, aes(x=clarity, fill=cut)) + geom_bar() + scale_y_log10(); print(example_1)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:18px;text-align:left\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:18px;text-align:left\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:18px;text-align:left\">not sure how to troubleshoot this one but hopefully someone else might,</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:18px;text-align:left\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:18px;text-align:left\">thanks,</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:18px;text-align:left\">zach cp</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:18px;text-align:left\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:18px;text-align:left\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:18px;text-align:left\"><br></span></div>"
