   "subject": "Re: axis issue when using scale_Y_log10()",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "This problem is probably related to using stacking with log scales. See here:<div><a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/issues/257\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/issues/257&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792376775858000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2OYm0xwa_zuaKNfnk3TS5z\">https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/issues/257</a></div><div><br></div><div>If you use position=&quot;dodge&quot;, it comes out as expected (I think):</div>\n\n<div>ggplot(diamonds, aes(x=clarity, fill=cut)) + geom_bar(position=&quot;dodge&quot;) + scale_y_log10() </div><div><br></div><div>-Winston<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Feb 29, 2012 at 2:09 PM, Zach Charlop-Powers <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">zach.char...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\n\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">HI everyone,<div><br></div><div>this is a direct report from stack overflor: <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/9502003/ggplot-scale-y-log10-issue\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/9502003/ggplot-scale-y-log10-issue&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792376775858000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3TbM_dF6T9DxpQwmBTflkD\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/9502003/ggplot-scale-y-log10-issue</a></div>\n\n<div><br></div><div>however I think the issue has reached the point where I think I have exposed a bug (as opposed to me not knowing how to use ggplot). basically the scale becomes wrong when the fill variable is different from the x-variable for ggplot bar graphs. In the following examples, example1 will have the appropriate scale but example 2 will  not: </div>\n\n<div><span style=\"line-height:18px;text-align:left;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"line-height:18px;text-align:left;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\">example_1 = ggplot(diamonds, aes(x=clarity, fill=clarity)) + geom_bar() + scale_y_log10(); print(example_1)</span><br>\n\n</div><div><span style=\"line-height:18px;text-align:left;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\">example_2 = ggplot(diamonds, aes(x=clarity, fill=cut)) + geom_bar() + scale_y_log10(); print(example_1)</span><span style=\"line-height:18px;text-align:left;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\"><br>\n\n</span></div><div><span style=\"line-height:18px;text-align:left;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"line-height:18px;text-align:left;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\">not sure how to troubleshoot this one but hopefully someone else might,</span></div>\n\n<div><span style=\"line-height:18px;text-align:left;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"line-height:18px;text-align:left;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\">thanks,</span></div>\n\n<div><span style=\"line-height:18px;text-align:left;font-size:14px;font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\">zach cp</span></div></blockquote></div></div>"
